  "purpose": "Control identifiers and official titles for the 800-53 Rev 5 controls this assessment exercises, plus the full Rev 5 family list. Used by the standalone NIST matrix so every row names the control the way the reader's own documentation, POA&M, and auditor do — a bare 'AC-6(9)' is not a deliverable.",
  "note": "Titles are the Rev 5 titles, which differ from Rev 4 in several places this assessment touches: AC-11 is 'Device Lock' (was 'Session Lock'), AT-2 is 'Literacy Training and Awareness' (was 'Security Awareness Training'), AU-2 is 'Event Logging' (was 'Audit Events'), AU-4 is 'Audit Log Storage Capacity', AC-6(9) is 'Log Use of Privileged Functions', and AC-16 gained 'and Privacy'. Citing a Rev 4 title under a Rev 5 heading is the kind of error an auditor notices first.",
